Below is one possible fix. The core issue is that GeoJSON “MultiPolygon” geometries sometimes contain empty inner‐ring arrays (`[]`), which leads to `deflateMultiCoordinatesArray()` producing an invalid last‐end index (e.g. `undefined`) and ultimately throwing “Invalid array length.” We can work around this by filtering out any empty rings before we hand the raw coordinates over to the `MultiPolygon` constructor (and hence to `setCoordinates`).

```javascript
### src/ol/format/GeoJSON.js
