```

Explanation:

- We locate the `readMultiPolygonGeometry` helper in `src/ol/format/GeoJSON.js`.
- Instead of passing `object['coordinates']` directly into the `MultiPolygon` constructor, we first run a `.map(...filter...)` to strip out any `ring` arrays of length zero.
- Now `setCoordinates()` inside the `MultiPolygon` class never receives an empty ring, so its call to `deflateMultiCoordinatesArray()` produces sane `endss` and avoids setting `this.flatCoordinates.length` to `undefined`.

With this one‐line change (plus the 3–lines of context around it) you should no longer see “Uncaught RangeError: Invalid array length” when reading your GeoJSON.
